+<dialog id="docs"><h2>A little composition goes a long way.</h2><p><strong>Intersection (AND)</strong> combines selectors with <code>:is()</code>. An element must match every selector to receive your styles.</p><p><strong>Union (OR)</strong> groups selectors in one <code>:is()</code> list. An element only needs to match one.</p><p>Conditions wrap your rule in <code>@media</code>, <code>@supports</code>, or <code>@container</code>. Intersection nests conditions so all must apply. Union creates a rule for each condition so any can apply.</p><p>Add selectors with Enter, edit the declarations, then copy your CSS. The preview uses your current viewport and browser capabilities; container conditions use the preview's width.</p><form method="dialog"><button>Got it</button></form></dialog>
